.TH DOKKU 1 "@DATE@" "Dokku @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dokku \- macOS-style dock and application launcher for XFCE4
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dokku
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dokku is a modern dock and full-screen application launcher designed for XFCE4,
featuring macOS-style magnification effects, app indicators, and a customizable
plugin system.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-launcher
Open the full-screen application launcher directly.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the settings window.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help information.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Dock Panel
Animated dock with magnification effect on hover, running app indicators,
and drag-and-drop icon reordering.
.TP
.B Application Launcher
Full-screen launchpad with grid view, real-time search, and keyboard navigation.
.TP
.B Pin/Unpin Apps
Right-click to pin running apps or unpin favorites from the dock.
.TP
.B Plugin System
Extensible architecture supporting custom dock plugins. Built-in plugins
include Trash, Show Desktop, and Separator.
.TP
.B Theming
Installable themes for dock customization. Themes are stored in
~/.local/share/dokku/themes/
.SH PLUGINS
Plugins are folders with a
.I plugin.ini
in
.I ~/.local/share/dokku/plugins/
(or in the data directories under
.IR dokku/plugins/ ,
where the Clock, Battery and Volume plugins ship; they start switched off). A
widget plugin shows text on its icon, from a strftime
.B format
or from the first line of a
.B script
(later lines become the tooltip). Other keys:
.BR interval ,
.BR command ,
.BR scroll_up ,
.BR scroll_down ,
.BR tooltip_format ,
.B hide_when_empty
and
.BR default_enabled .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dokku/config.ini
User configuration file containing pinned apps, dock settings, and enabled plugins.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dokku/config.ini.bak
The settings that the last Import or Reset replaced.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/dokku/themes/
User-installed themes directory.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dokku/themes/
System-wide themes directory.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in INI format. Example:
.PP
.nf
[Dock]
pinned=org.gnome.Nautilus;firefox;org.gnome.Terminal
icon_size=48
magnification=1.5
auto_hide=false
position=bottom
theme=default

[Plugins]
enabled=trash;show-desktop

[Media]
blocked_players=firefox;chromium;chrome

[Launcher]
web_search_url=https://duckduckgo.com/?q=%s
.fi
.PP
The media widget follows the MPRIS2 player that is playing, and keeps it until
another player starts. Players whose D-Bus name contains a word in
.B blocked_players
are ignored. The default list covers common web browsers. An empty list ignores
nothing. The same list is under Settings, Behavior, Ignored players.
.PP
In the launcher's search box, a calculation such as 2+3*4 shows its answer and
recent files that match are listed. When no app matches, a row searches the web
at
.B web_search_url
(%s stands for the search words; an empty value turns the row off).
.SH THEME FORMAT
Themes use INI format with the following sections:
.PP
.nf
[Theme]
name=My Theme

[Background]
red=0.15
green=0.15
blue=0.15
alpha=0.75

[Border]
red=1.0
green=1.0
blue=1.0
alpha=0.15

[Indicator]
red=1.0
green=1.0
blue=1.0
alpha=0.9

[Style]
corner_radius=16
border_width=1
.fi
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Escape
Close the application launcher.
.TP
.B Any key
Focus search bar in launcher and start typing.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for XFCE4 desktop environment.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at: https://github.com/yarisgutierrez/Dokku/issues
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xfce4-panel (1)
